999	    /// Spec (pinning current, deliberate behavior): `commit_touches_pathspecs`
1000	    /// configures `track_rewrites(None)`, so renames are never reported as a
1001	    /// single `Change::Rewrite` -- gix instead reports them as a separate
1002	    /// `Deletion` (old path) and `Addition` (new path). This test renames a
1003	    /// file *out of* a pathspec-matching directory into a non-matching one
1004	    /// and asserts the rename commit is still reported as touching the
1005	    /// pathspec, because the `Deletion` at the old (matching) location is
1006	    /// enough to trip `change_matches_pathspecs` on its own -- independent of
1007	    /// whether the new location matches anything.
